<title>UK: Volatile currencies restrict UK meals trading.</title>
<headline>Volatile currencies restrict UK meals trading.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Continued volatile trading on the currency markets kept most players on the sidelines of the UK meals and feeds market on Thursday.</p>
<p>Higher soymeal prices discouraged buyers with sellers one to two stg higher.</p>
<p>In limited trading A.D.M rapemeal fetched 125 stg a tonne for January ex-mill Erith.</p>
<p>Palmkernel pellets traded at 76 stg a tonne for spot ex-store Newport.</p>
<p>--Jim Ballantyne, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8062</p>
</text>
